# Copy to .env.local for local development. In production (e.g. Vercel), set
# these as real environment variables in the project dashboard instead —
# never commit actual values here.
#
# Get these from your Supabase project: Project Settings -> API.
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the public "anon"/"publishable" key — safe to
# expose client-side. Never use the service_role key here.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# AI multi-view generation (optional). Server-only — deliberately NOT
# VITE_-prefixed, so these never reach the browser bundle; the client only
# ever calls the server function in src/server-functions/multiview.ts, which
# reads these and proxies to your real service. Leave unset to run with
# today's depth-only reconstruction — the app detects this and reports
# "Multi-view AI provider is not configured" rather than faking results.
#
# Point MULTIVIEW_API_URL at a service implementing the job contract
# documented at the top of src/server-functions/multiview.ts (POST /jobs,
# GET /jobs/:id, POST /jobs/:id/cancel) — e.g. your own deployment of a
# multi-view diffusion model (Wonder3D, Zero123++, etc.) behind a GPU worker,
# or a hosted multi-view generation API.
MULTIVIEW_API_URL=
MULTIVIEW_API_KEY=
MULTIVIEW_MODEL=
